    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 62\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5475, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the state finance law, in relation to five-year\n      capital plans for the state university of New York  and  the  city\n      university of New York\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  require the Governor to submit annually, as part of\nthe Executive Budget proposal, five-year capital  plans  for  the  State\nUniversity  of New York and the City University of New York covering one\nhundred percent of the  capital  maintenance  costs  identified  by  the\nUniversity systems.\n \n  This  bill  was previously vetoed in 2015, 2017, and 2018 for the same\nstructural legal reason: it would violate the provisions  of  the  State\nConstitution.\n \n  Article  VII of the New York State Constitution grants to the Governor\nthe duty to  determine  the  proposed  expenditures  and  appropriations\nincluded  within  the  Executive  Budget  submitted  to the Legislature.\nRequiring the inclusion in the Executive Budget Proposal  of  a  capital\nplan  and annual appropriations established by the SUNY and CUNY systems\nwould be an attempt to legislatively  remove  this  authority  from  the\nGovernor and place it into the hands of administrative boards, in direct\nviolation of Article VII.\n \n  Moreover,  giving  statutory priority to higher education capital over\nall other capital needs would exacerbate current  debt  cap  limitations\nand  have a detrimental impact on capital funding levels for other State\nprograms, such as housing and the environment.\n \n  It should be highlighted that the State has made  significant  invest-\nments  in  SUNY  and  CUNY  facilities. During the period from FY2012 to\nFY2022, $13.7 billion in new capital appropriations  have  been  enacted\nfor  our public colleges and universities. The FY2021 and FY2022 Enacted\nBudgets each provided $550 million for SUNY and $284 million for CUNY in\nannual capital maintenance funding, and the State's FY2022 Enacted Budg-\net Capital Plan assumes that  these  funding  levels  will  continue  in\nfuture years.\n \n  For these reasons, I must veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
